WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:02.910
ROBERT KUBIS: With almost
500 sessions at Next 2018,

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.707
it's understandable that you
couldn't get to them all.

00:00:05.707 --> 00:00:07.290
So if you didn't see
Building Scalable

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.970
Apps with Cloud
Firestore, then stay tuned

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:11.130
because here is the Rewind.

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.377
When it comes to
application development,

00:00:20.377 --> 00:00:22.460
I don't want to deal with
building and maintaining

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.300
infrastructure.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.500
Do you?

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.540
Cloud Firestore and
Firebase platform

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.670
lets you focus on
building your application

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:31.730
while Google Cloud is taking
care of the infrastructure.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:35.420
We believe this enables small
teams to accomplish big things

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.300
with powerful yet simple tools.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.450
This starts with the choice of
a wide range of Firebase SDKs

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:44.990
for Android, iOS, and
web to connect directly

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:46.460
to Cloud Firestore.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:48.530
The integration
with Firebase Auth

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.140
lets you setup authentication
and user management

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:54.350
in an easy way and integrates
with our declarative security

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:55.730
rules language.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:58.200
That allows you to control
access to your data,

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.100
not only based on the user but
also on the information that's

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.080
stored in your database.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.540
For storing and serving
your static content,

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.700
you can use Firebase Hosting.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.070
And finally, to run
server side logic

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.890
and expand into other
services on Google Cloud,

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:16.240
Cloud Firestore is integrated
with Cloud Functions.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.810
But we don't stop there.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.600
Cloud Firestore is not just
a database for mobile and web

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.960
applications.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.780
We also offer a full suite
of server client libraries

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.570
including libraries for C
Sharp, Go, Java, Python, and PHP

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:33.480
to enable powerful and more
complex backend applications.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:37.520
Next, Dennis talks about what
is new of Cloud Firestore.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:39.530
First, there are a
lot of new locations

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.660
that are rolling
out throughout 2019,

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:44.400
so you can store your data
closest to your users.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.580
Second, there is
a Datastore mode.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:49.370
Datastore mode allows you to
use your existing applications

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:51.380
built with Cloud
Datastore client libraries

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.660
on Cloud Firestore.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.980
And the best thing, your
existing applications

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:57.050
are going to be upgraded
from Cloud Datastore

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.560
seamlessly with no downtime
once Cloud Firestore graduates

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.660
to general availability.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.820
As a side note here,
this will probably

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.800
be the biggest
live data migration

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.320
with no downtime in history.

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.870
Third, we are removing
many of the Cloud Datastore

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:12.980
restrictions.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:15.680
No more one write per
second per entity group.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.110
No more Ancestor Only
Queries for consistency.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.510
You now gets strong consistency
across all your data

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:21.770
and complex queries.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:25.970
And no more 25 entity groups
per transaction limitation.

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:29.650
Fourth, there are a lot of
new tools and services coming.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:31.430
Fully managed
exports and imports

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:34.220
to and from cloud
storage seamless imports

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:37.400
of your backups into BigQuery
to enable further analytics,

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.950
and a flexible index
management from the UI

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.440
and many, many,
many more things.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.990
One more word on the
Datastore versus native mode.

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:47.660
Cloud Firestore can be used
in these two different modes

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.290
but not at the same time.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.860
So you need to make
a choice upfront.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:54.830
Datastore mode is used for
backwards compatibility

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.390
and high writes
throughput applications,

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:59.960
whereas native mode is
best used as a backend

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.570
as a service for mobile
and web applications,

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:04.220
which allows you
for synchronization

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.230
of state between
multiple devices

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:08.730
up to millions of
concurrent users.

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.850
If you want to know how
some of our customers

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:12.800
are using Cloud
Firestore, then learn

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.860
from Guesswork who built ML
[INAUDIBLE] e-commerce platform

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.570
on Cloud Firestore to
help companies like Zalora

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:21.260
with product recommendations.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.600
Or Hawken Dynamics,
which focuses

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:26.990
on analyzing sports performance
with hardware and software

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:29.490
to optimize athletic
performance.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:33.560
And finally, Notary, who
built the Next 2018 conference

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.650
website and mobile app
using Cloud Firestore.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:38.450
All of these use
cases give insights

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.730
into their architecture
and best practices

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:43.280
using Cloud Firestore.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.900
The second half
of the talk dives

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.750
into notable, awesome,
and exciting demos shown

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:50.330
and walked through by Cloud
Firestore to engineer Kathy Li.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.380
So please check that out.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:54.080
So if this sparked
your interest,

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.880
please watch the full talk.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.930
Links are in the
description below.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:00.410
And don't forget to subscribe
to the Google Cloud YouTube

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:02.992
channel for more great
Next Rewind content.

00:04:02.992 --> 00:04:03.950
Thank you for watching.

